The sum of three consecutive odd numbers is 69. What is the smallest of the three numbers ?
Let $n$ be the smallest of the three numbers.  Then, the sum of the three numbers is $n+(n+2)+(n+4)=69$.  Solving for $n$, we have \begin{align*}
n+(n+2)+(n+4)&=69\\
\Rightarrow\qquad 3n+6&=69\\
\Rightarrow\qquad 3n&=63\\
\Rightarrow\qquad n&=\boxed{21}
\end{align*}
Final Answer: The final answer is 21. I hope it is correct.
